- `python3 tools/reference/hit-test-probe.py /tmp/bt3-hit-test-probe.swf` emits a project-authored 970-byte AVM2 Sprite probe, SHA256 `263a0b80ceecf77d808008b61cdd86a944f7b7eca337d01efc6746134d0a66b3`. The served response was independently checked against that hash. REA controlled replay `ev_fdec9ed43dd86ad0fed95fd46706cea349a57315f04606b22e71a677b4360a1e` loaded it through the local viewer with npm Ruffle 0.7.1/wgpu-webgl and observed all 13 expected results plus completion. After the child is hidden or made alpha-zero, both parent and child queries remain true. Transparent fill and outer-stroke queries also hit; explicit Sprite masks constrain hits, a mask-only parent does not hit, and queries after removal are false. The probe does not independently hide the root, execute game combat, test every display-object class or establish Adobe behavior. The capture reports complete scoped coverage and browser cleanup; its runtime artifact identity is not supplied by REA, so the route/hash observation is separate provenance.
- The viewer now registers `traceObserver` after Ruffle's `load` creates its runtime instance, preserving first-frame diagnostics. The prior early setter silently lost them. The replay recorded no page errors, and its owned browser and local port 3104 server were closed. Full evidence remains local under ignored `reference-captures/body-timelines/`; no generated SWF is committed.
- At the body-timeline checkpoint, the alpha-contact provider and hidden-body exclusions still differed from this contract. The geometric-contact checkpoint below replaces those exclusions and adds attached native effects. Earlier image/contact tests alone did not establish original collision parity.

### Procedural body timelines

- All 20 catalog body roots now use retained source timelines and 12 fitted blue leaf approximations. The repeatable import contains 109 sprites, 25 shape-bound records, 5097 placements and 24 painted leaf descriptions. Normal, dark and light bodies keep distinct source colors and glints. Three one-frame Huge Base variants remain static; the other 17 body roots animate.
- Gameplay, previews, drafts, placed designs and forcefield silhouettes share those retained body clips. This includes 40-frame breathing and recovered Wiggle, Air Bladder, Tentacle, Smooth Tentacle and Sliding Cluster motion. The longest root has340 frames; child phases, root branches and jumps remain independent. Posters and stopped-frame class captures compose the same fitted leaves. Smooth Tentacle's rounded random start can resolve to an empty frame 1; empty artwork keeps zero Script bounds and a transparent poster, preserving the initial creator measurement in both asset modes.
- Two fresh imports reproduce leaf SHA256 `4e89e1ba82527efbafca11b8cf5a13d26ed39b00b3dc4c80f6eb59e2b1dc1d00` and timeline SHA256 `7bfd5c4d921da2ec2135343e552b34dadddcd72ac6c32806f8a240bbf782ed5c`. Numeric fields are finite; no original media or vector contours are committed. The old mock-assets check expected a translucent placeholder body. Direct sampling now confirms blue, fully opaque center pixels in both the supplied-SWF and procedural Large Bubble posters, and checks both against alpha 255. Independent half-opacity tank/weapon checks remain. Exact contours, antialiasing, global random/event ordering and the collision audit above remain fidelity boundaries.
- Incremental landing verification: formatting, TypeScript, all 411 rule/parser tests with 5516 assertions and the production build pass. All 16 affected native/mock body, weapon, creator, class, damage and protection browser cases pass. After correcting the source-backed opacity check, the complete 44-case mock/synthetic selection passes in one run. Both body/creator galleries were inspected. The probe regenerated and replayed successfully with 13 expected results and no page errors. Local captures, raw evidence and a provenance manifest remain under ignored `reference-captures/body-timelines/`. These checks establish the stated animation and sizing contracts; the geometric-contact gap and complete game parity remain open.

### Geometry contour export groundwork

- `shapeHitGeometry` exposes parsed fill/stroke contours for the upcoming geometric-contact adapter. It preserves shape registration, original pixel units, drawing layers, fill winding and stroke width/cap/join/miter facts. Transparent styles still contribute geometry. The export reuses the parser's run stitching and carries no paint colors or filter output.
- The new rule check covers a transparent filled/stroked rectangle, nonzero winding, original registration and line attributes. Formatting, TypeScript and all 412 rule/parser tests with 5519 assertions pass. The following integration must connect these contours to retained tank parts, masks and attached effects; the collision mismatch recorded above remains open at this groundwork stage.


